@* DS parity — no consumer yet. The design system still ships components/StatTile, but its
   last consumer in the app was the Budgets record's Expected / Actual balance pair, and the
   RecordCard rollout replaced that with two OdsInfoTiles in the Details grid — a labelled tile
   per figure rather than a bare one. Kept, not deleted: StatTile is the overview/dashboard
   figure, and the next overview band that needs one should find it here. *@

@*
    OdsStatTile — a headline statistic tile (Odyssey Design System · components/StatTile).

    An overline label, a tabular-monospace headline figure, and an optional
    delta line. DeltaDir tints the delta up (income green) or down (expense
    coral). The standard Dashboard / overview figure.
*@

<div class="odc-stat">
    @if (Overline is not null)
    {
        <div class="odc-stat-overline">@Overline</div>
    }
    <div class="odc-stat-num @ValueClassName">@Value</div>
    @if (Delta is not null)
    {
        <div class="odc-stat-delta @DeltaClass">@Delta</div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Small uppercase label above the figure.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Overline { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The headline figure (rendered tabular monospace).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? Value { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optional change line below the figure.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Delta { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Tints the delta: Up = income green, Down = expense coral.</summary>
    [Parameter] public OdsDeltaDirection? DeltaDir { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Tints the figure itself — income / expense — for a balance that flips sign.</summary>
    [Parameter] public OdsValueTone? ValueClass { get; set; }

    private string ValueClassName => ValueClass switch
    {
        OdsValueTone.Income => "income",
        OdsValueTone.Expense => "expense",
        _ => string.Empty,
    };

    private string DeltaClass => DeltaDir switch
    {
        OdsDeltaDirection.Up => "up",
        OdsDeltaDirection.Down => "down",
        _ => string.Empty,
    };
}
